/-!
# Common-field commutators in the terminal Cartan argument

The source complements have a nonzero central commutator. The canonical
compatible field on P makes this an actual field subspace of both P and V
with agreeing scalars. The two literal Cartan subgroups fix the opposite
complements, and commuting actors preserve the scalar on displacement images.

The full scalar spectra of these Cartan subgroups and the generator and
weights for X ∩ K remain to be constructed. The obstruction adapter keeps
these obligations explicit; this module does not claim Proposition 11.3.2.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), 11.3.8--9
and the final paragraph of Proposition 11.3.2, printed p.775.
-/
